jobs.description:
About the role

Lift Schools is looking for an employer brand and recruitment marketing lead to join our marketing, communications and content team. This role brings together marketing expertise, authentic storytelling and recruitment strategy to help us attract brilliant people to work across our schools.

You'll shape how we share what makes Lift Schools a rewarding place to work. From building our Employer Value Proposition (EVP) to creating engaging digital content and managing targeted campaigns, you'll bring our culture and our colleagues' stories to life.

This role sits at the heart of our mission: ensuring every child receives an excellent education, in every classroom, every day.

Key responsibilities

You will:

* help shape and embed our Employer Value Proposition (EVP) through authentic, human-centred storytelling that positions Lift Schools as an employer of choice;
* plan and manage our organic social media calendar across LinkedIn and other platforms, creating engaging copy and graphics that spotlight our people, values and workplace culture;
* identify compelling colleague stories and turn them into creative briefs for video content, working with our senior designer and external freelancers on filming and editing;
* produce fresh storytelling content such as employee profiles and career progression journeys, and optimise our careers websites for candidate experience and search visibility;
* plan and run paid digital advertising campaigns to generate applications for high priority roles and Initial Teacher Training (ITT) programmes, managing budgets to achieve the best return; and
* monitor the effectiveness of all recruitment marketing activity, using data insights to create clear recommendations for senior stakeholders.

What we're looking for

You will have:

* 3 to 5 years of relevant background in digital marketing, recruitment marketing or employer branding;
* hands-on skills creating social-first copy and graphics using tools like Canva, alongside writing creative briefs and guiding video production;
* a track record planning and managing organic social media content that brings workplace culture to life;
* the ability to update and optimise careers websites with a strong focus on user experience, conversion and basic SEO principles;
* strong analytical skills, using web and social analytics to track return on investment and translate insights into practical recommendations; and
* excellent communication skills, with the ability to work effectively across teams including recruitment, ITT and schools.

You'll be a natural storyteller with genuine curiosity for finding authentic colleague stories and turning them into relatable digital content. You're highly organised, proactive and confident balancing quick-turnaround campaigns with longer-term brand strategy. Could this be the perfect opportunity to combine your creative and analytical skills in a role that really matters?

Regular travel between schools is required, so you'll need a full UK driving licence and access to a vehicle. Mileage for travel between schools during the working day will be reimbursed from your base location.

Who is Lift Schools?

Lift Schools is made up of 62 primary, secondary and special schools, educating more than 35,000 pupils across the country. We believe education can transform lives - and we want every child in our schools to achieve their full potential.

How we support you

We want you to feel supported, valued and able to grow throughout your career with Lift Schools. From high-quality professional development and career progression to wellbeing support and opportunities to connect and collaborate across our network, we invest in you so you can do your best work. Discover how we'll support you to thrive, develop and grow your career in the way that's right for you: How we support you.
